{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/295419-uses-of-fleeting-summer","id":295419,"title":"Uses of Fleeting Summer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-28T17:31:56-07:00","id":295419,"title":"Uses of Fleeting Summer","content":"So, we have a character, going for Sun's Tongue. They decided that, hey, the could grab some of the Fleeting Summer contracts. Half way through reading them, the player decided that they were only good for &quot;picking fights.&quot; <br /> <br /> So, I'm just curious. What are the various uses you've put the Fleeting Summer powers to use, and help encourage the player?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T18:42:04-07:00","id":295499,"title":"","content":"At least one of Fleeting Summer's contracts (the one that lets you quell anger in an area) is good for *preventing* fights. <br /> <br /> You can find the strongest source of anger in an area, and use that anger to manipulate him.<br /> <br /> You can act as a firebrand to inspire social reform through group effort (or mobs to cause a distraction).<br /> <br /> You can sow dissension among an enemy group my making them all angry at you, then redirecting that anger at one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T14:44:20-07:00","id":297520,"title":"","content":"The final clauses lets you stir yourself into implacable battle rage that gives +2/+4 die to physical rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T18:23:58-07:00","id":297663,"title":"","content":"Oh, you can wait until your enemy is about to give a big angry speech, then redirect his anger to be at poodles and watch him make an idiot of himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T21:51:55-08:00","id":302974,"title":"","content":"Fleeting Summer is really good for a diplomat 'ling. 4 makes it so that you can say all sorts of things without angering people, 3 lets you turn your opponent in a debate into a sputtering pile of rage, 2 lets you play with the emotions of the crowd and so on. All the fleeting contracts are good for letting you play with people's emotions like they're nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}